# Security Phase 6 (ADR 0033): Netlify-native header injection for the public demo
# deployment specifically. web-ui/nginx.conf (ADR 0029) covers the docker-compose
# deployment, which Netlify never runs — Netlify serves this directory as a static
# site straight from its own CDN, so this project needs its own equivalent here.
#
# Tighter than nginx.conf's CSP on purpose, not just a copy: connect-src only lists
# the one real backend this deployment ever calls (Render's rag-service URL) —
# never the local docker-compose ports (8081/8082/8084), which mean nothing on the
# public internet and would just be misleading noise here. The demo has no
# upload/auth flow at all (DemoSecurityConfig, ADR 0020), so ingestion-service and
# auth-service origins are correctly absent, not an oversight.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self' https://ag-service-demo.onrender.com; img-src 'self' data:; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# No content hashing in this static, no-build-step web-ui, so index.html/style.css/
# app.js keep the same URL across deploys. Netlify's CDN (and browsers) can then
# keep serving an old style.css/app.js against a freshly deployed HTML shell unless
# told to always revalidate — the exact staleness this project already hit once
# with the demo serving an outdated build (ADR 0033).
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
/style.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
/app.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
